  <div class="prose-til">
    <p>
      <strong>TilBlog</strong> captures lessons from real LLM conversations —
      the framing that worked, the wrong turn that clarified things, and the mental model worth keeping.
    </p>
    <p>
      Posts are organized like course tracks
      (<em>Problem Solving 101</em>, <em>Signal Processing 202</em>, …)
      even though they come from messy chats, not a syllabus.
    </p>
    <h2>How a lesson is written</h2>
    <p>Each note aims for one reusable insight: the question, what clicked, the pitfall, and the rule to keep.</p>
    <h2>Built with</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Eleventy</strong> — Markdown to static HTML</li>
      <li><strong>Tailwind CSS</strong> — compile-time styles + Typography</li>
      <li><strong>Alpine.js</strong> — small bundled interactions</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</article>
